Hi Luke,
Until I have time-dependent raster (time-stack/brick) support, yes this would be the approach.
You can fit one movement model (and UD) to the same seasons over multiple years, as long as the puma did not migrate/disperse or radically change behavior in some other way. The gaps do not impede the calculation - they just make the variogram ugly where there is no data.
That's what I would do, unless the seasonal data were very limited and space use across season was not very variable.
Best,
Chris

